  62:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h **** /**
  63:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  * @addtogroup CCU4
  64:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  * @brief Capture Compare Unit 4 (CCU4) low level driver for XMC family of microcontrollers<br>
  65:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  *
  66:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  * The CCU4 peripheral is a major component for systems that need general purpose timers for signal
  67:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  * monitoring/conditioning and Pulse Width Modulation (PWM) signal generation. Power electronic con
  68:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  * switched mode power supplies or interruptible power supplies, can easily be implemented with the
  69:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  * CCU4 peripheral.\n
  70:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  * Each CCU4 module is comprised of four identical 16 bit Capture/Compare Timer slices, CC4y (where
  71:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  * timer slice can work in compare mode or in capture mode.
  72:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  *
  73:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  * APIs provided in this file cover the following functional blocks of CCU4:\n
  74:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  * -- Timer configuration, Capture configuration, Function/Event configuration, Interrupt configura
  75:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  * \par Note:
  76:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  * 1. SLICE (APIs prefixed with e.g. XMC_CCU4_SLICE_)\n
  77:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  * 2. Module (APIs are not having any prefix e.g. XMC_CCU4_) \n
  78:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  *
  79:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  * \par Timer(Compare mode) configuration:\n
  80:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  * This section of the LLD provides the configuration structure XMC_CCU4_SLICE_COMPARE_CONFIG_t and
  81:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  * function XMC_CCU4_SLICE_CompareInit().\n
  82:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  *
  83:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  * It can be used to:
  84:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  * -# Start and Stop the timer. (XMC_CCU4_SLICE_StartTimer(), XMC_CCU4_SLICE_StopTimer())
  85:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  * -# Update the period, compare, Dither, Prescaler  and Passive values. (XMC_CCU4_SLICE_SetTimerPe
  86:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  *    XMC_CCU4_SLICE_SetTimerCompareMatch(), XMC_CCU4_SLICE_SetPrescaler(), XMC_CCU4_SLICE_SetDithe
  87:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  *    XMC_CCU4_SLICE_SetPassiveLevel())
  88:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  * -# Enable the slices to support multichannel mode. (XMC_CCU4_SLICE_EnableMultiChannelMode())
  89:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  * 
  90:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  * \par Capture configuration:\n
  91:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  * This section of the LLD provides the configuration structure XMC_CCU4_SLICE_CAPTURE_CONFIG_t and
  92:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  * function XMC_CCU4_SLICE_CaptureInit().\n
  93:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  *
  94:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  * It can be used to:
  95:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  * -# Configure the capture functionality. (XMC_CCU4_SLICE_Capture0Config(), XMC_CCU4_SLICE_Capture
  96:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  * -# Read the captured values along with the status, which indicate the value is latest or not.
  97:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  *    (XMC_CCU4_SLICE_GetCaptureRegisterValue())
  98:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  * 
  99:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  * \par Function/Event configuration:\n
 100:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  * This section of the LLD provides the configuration structure XMC_CCU4_SLICE_EVENT_CONFIG_t.\n
 101:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  * 
 102:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  * It can be used to:
 103:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  * -# Enable and Disable the events. (XMC_CCU4_SLICE_EnableEvent(), XMC_CCU4_SLICE_DisableEvent())
 104:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  * -# Configure to start and stop the timer on external events.(XMC_CCU4_SLICE_StartConfig(), XMC_C
 105:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  * -# Modulation, external load and Gating of the timer output.(XMC_CCU4_SLICE_ModulationConfig(), 
 106:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  *    XMC_CCU4_SLICE_LoadConfig(), XMC_CCU4_SLICE_GateConfig())
 107:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  * -# Control the count direction of the timer based on the external event. (XMC_CCU4_SLICE_Directi
 108:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  * -# Count the external events.(XMC_CCU4_SLICE_CountConfig())
 109:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  * -# External Trap. Which can be used as protective feature.(XMC_CCU4_SLICE_EnableTrap(), XMC_CCU4
 110:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  *    XMC_CCU4_SLICE_TrapConfig())
 111:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  *
 112:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  * \par Interrupt configuration:\n
 113:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  * This section of the LLD provides the function to configure the interrupt node to each event (XMC
 114:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  * @{
 115:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  */
