1098:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  * Configures the Trap Function of the slice, by configuring CC4yCMC.TS, CC4yTC.TRPSE, and CC4yTC.T
1099:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  * Trap function is mapped with Event-2. Criteria for exiting the trap state is configured.
1100:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  * This trap function allows PWM outputs to react on the state of an input pin.
1101:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  * Thus PWM output can be forced to inactive state upon detection of a trap.
1102:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  * It is also possible to synchronize the trap function with the PWM signal using the \b synch_with
1103:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu4.h ****  *
